t transformersâ€","â€œHotFlip: White-Box Adversarial Examples for Text Classificationâ€","â€œUniversal Adversarial Triggers for Attacking and Analyzing NLP.â€","code","â€œRobust Conversational Agents against Imperceptible Toxicity Triggers.â€","â€œUniversal and Transferable Adversarial Attacks on Aligned Language Models.â€","â€œRLPrompt: Optimizing Discrete Text Prompts with Reinforcement Learning.â€","â€œIs BERT Really Robust? A Strong Baseline for Natural Language Attack on Text Classification and Entailment.â€","â€œBERT-Attack: Adversarial Attack Against BERT Using BERT.â€","\"TextAttack: A Framework for Adversarial Attacks, Data Augmentation, and Adversarial Training in NLP.\"","â€œBot-Adversarial Dialogue for Safe Conversational Agents.â€","â€œAdversarial training for high-stakes reliability.â€","â€œRed Teaming Language Models to Reduce Harms: Methods, Scaling Behaviors, and Lessons Learned.â€","â€œRed Teaming Language Models with Language Models.â€","â€œRed Teaming Language Models to Reduce Harms: Methods, Scaling Behaviors, and Lessons Learned.â€","â€œFLIRT: Feedback Loop In-context Red Teaming.â€","â€œExplore, Establish, Exploit: Red Teaming Language Models from Scratch.â€","â€œDefending ChatGPT against Jailbreak Attack via Self-Reminder.â€","â€œAutomatically Auditing Large Language Models via Discrete Optimization.â€","â€œCompromising Real-World LLM-Integrated Applications with Indirect Prompt Injection.â€","â€œBaseline Defenses for Adversarial Attacks Against Aligned Language Models.â€","â€œJailbroken: How Does LLM Safety Training Fail?â€","â€œEDA: Easy data augmentation techniques for boosting performance on text classification tasks.â€","www.jailbreakchat.com","â€œYou can use GPT-4 to create prompt injections against GPT-4â€","Nlp","Language-Model","Safety","Adversarial Attacks","Robustness","Redteam"],"chroma:document":"Redteam","emphasized_text_contents":["black box","What","NOUN","â†’Which","NOUN","WP","is â†’","WP","â€™sâ€™","wasâ†’is","GBDA","make adversarial loss optimization differentiable","extreme","â€œa similarity score for evaluating text generation that captures the semantic similarity between pairwise tokens in contextualized embeddings of a transformer model.â€","HotFlip","Universal Adversarial Triggers","UAT","AutoPrompt","UAT-LM","UTSC","unigram","affirmative","greedy coordinate gradient (GCG)","transferability","ARCA","coordinate ascent","should have been mitigated","Competing objective","Mismatched generalization","Display of saliency score of each token","Token substitution and insertion","Zero-shot generation","Stochastic few-shot generation","Supervised learning","Reinforcement learning","Explore","Establish","Exploit","FLIRT","update in-context exemplars","FIFO","LIFO","the last one","Scoring","effectiveness","diversity","low-toxicity","Scoring-LIFO","robust","inner maximization","outer minimization","Inner maximization","Outer minimization","instruct","adversarial training","Paraphrase","Retokenization"],"url":"https://lilianweng.github.io/posts/2023-10-25-adv-attack-llm/"}␀␀␀\pi}_i^{(j)} = \\frac{\\exp(\\frac{\\Theta_{ij} + g_{ij}}{\\tau})}{\\sum_{v=1}^V \\exp(\\frac{\\Theta_{iv} + g_{iv}}{\\tau})} $$\n\nwhere $g_{ij} \\sim \\text{Gumbel}(0, 1)$; the temperature $\\tau > 0$ controls the smoothness of the distribution.\n\nGumbel distribution is used to model the extreme value, maximum or minimum, of a number of samples, irrespective of the sample distribution. The additional Gumbel noise brings in the stochastic decisioning that mimic the sampling process from the categorical distribution.\n\nA low temperature $\\tau \\to 0$ pushes the convergence to categorical distribution, since sampling from softmax with temperature 0 is deterministic. The â€œsamplingâ€ portion only depends on the value of $g_{ij}$, which is mostly centered around 0."}␀␀␀0—ŠFy␀␀␀	␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ •ŠFy␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀p•ŠFy␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀”ŠFy␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀p”ŠFy␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ ”ŠFy␀␀␀