\arg\\min_{\\mathbf{t}} \\mathbb{E}_{\\mathbf{x}\\sim\\mathcal{D}} [\\mathcal{L}_\\text{adv}(\\tilde{y}, f([\\mathbf{t}; \\mathbf{x}]))] $$","url":"https://lilianweng.github.io/posts/2023-10-25-adv-attack-llm/","link_texts":["#","Morris et al. 2020","Ribeiro et al (2018)","EDA","Wei & Zou 2019","Jin et al. 2019","Li et al. 2020","#","Guo et al. 2021","Jang et al. 2016","Zhang et al. 2019","Ebrahimi et al. 2018","Wallace et al. (2019)","HotFlip","Shin et al., 2020","Mehrabi et al. (2022)","Zou et al. (2023)","OpenAI 2023","UAT and AutoPrompt","Jones et al. 2023","#","Wei et al. (2023)","DAN","AIM","it can understand","Wei et al. (2023)","Greshake et al. (2023)","#","Wallace et al. (2019)","QuizBowl QA dataset","Ziegler et al. (2022)","Wallace et al. (2019)","BERT-Attack","Xu et al. 2021","BAD dataset","Tensorflow dataset","red-teaming dataset","Ganguli, et al. 2022","GPT-4","DALL-E 3","#","Perez et al. 2022","A2C","BAD (Bot Adversarial Dialogue) dataset","nucleus sampling","Casper et al. (2023)","Perez et al. (2022)","here","here","here","Mehrabi et al. 2023","in-context learning","Perez et al. 2022","Schramowski et al. 2022","https://github.com/notAI-tech/NudeNet)","Perspective API","#","#","Madry et al. 2017","#","Xie et al. 2023","Jain et al. 2023","White-box attacks","UAT-LM","Jain et al. 2023","#","#","â€œTowards Deep Learning Models Resistant to Adversarial Attacksâ€","â€œSemantically equivalent adversarial rules for debugging NLP modelsâ€","â€œGradient-based adversarial attacks against text transformersâ€","â€œHotFlip: White-Box Adversarial Examples for Text Classificationâ€","â€œUniversal Adversarial Triggers for Attacking and Analyzing NLP.â€","code","â€œRobust Conversational Agents against Imperceptible Toxicity Triggers.â€","â€œUniversal and Transferable Adversarial Attacks on Aligned Language Models.â€","â€œRLPrompt: Optimizing Discrete Text Prompts with Reinforcement Learning.â€","â€œIs BERT Really Robust? A Strong Baseline for Natural Language A